  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amal Kasserine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In light of mounting political and social pressures, civil society organizations and actors face a growing challenge in restoring meaning through the formulation of alternative narratives that reflect their reality and experiences, as opposed to the official narrative that feeds on demonization, betrayal, and the suppression of independent initiatives (Authorities often tend to present civil society as an intruder or a puppet).  From this perspective, there is a need to empower associations with tools for documentation, expression, and meaning-making that enhance their resilience and enable them to construct their own narratives that highlight their actual social role and develop their ability to counter discourses of exclusion and betrayal. To achieve the initiative&apos;s goals, we will work to understand and deconstruct the official narrative around civil action as a whole and identify its objectives. Then we will work to enable associations to capitalize on their projects, clarify their objectives, and market the impact of their initiativesso that they can refute the false accusations against them. From there, we will move into the public sphere to encourage young people to engage in civic action and contribute to building a livable city through simple activities that support the links between associations, as well as with young people who want to exercise their citizenship.  The most important added value of this initiative isbuilding the confidence of association leaders in their leadership role, especially in times of tyranny, in perseverance, and in raising the level of struggle among the people for a just and democratic state where there is no room for exclusion.Translated with DeepL.com (free version)</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="23">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Association Amal pour la solidarit&#xE9;</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">La cr&#xE9;ation de l&#x2019;association AMAL, le 19 F&#xE9;vrier 2011, est venue suite aux &#xE9;v&#xE9;nements ayant secou&#xE9; Kasserine &#xE0; la veille de la r&#xE9;volution glorieuse, en cons&#xE9;quence au r&#xF4;le important qu&#x2019;ont tenu certains individus dans la protection de la ville, et en r&#xE9;ponse &#xE0; lan&#xE9;cessit&#xE9; de penser &#xE0; mettre ces efforts dans un cadre l&#xE9;gal.
L&#x2019;association &#xE9;t&#xE9; fond&#xE9;e par un groupe d&#x2019;activistes, avec pour but premier de prot&#xE9;ger les objectifs de la r&#xE9;volution (dignit&#xE9;, libert&#xE9;, emploi&#x2026;). Par la suite, les efforts de l&#x2019;association ont &#xE9;t&#xE9; orient&#xE9;s vers la sensibilisation des citoyens, vu l&#x2019;importance du d&#xE9;veloppement humain pour l&#x2019;avenir du gouvernorat.
D&#xE9;veloppementale et culturelle, sp&#xE9;cialis&#xE9;e dans les domaines de l&#x2019;&#xE9;ducation sociale et le d&#xE9;veloppement intellectuel, l&#x2019;Association AMAL pour la solidarit&#xE9;,le D&#xE9;veloppement et le savoir &#xE0; Kasserine est la premi&#xE8;re association ayant obtenu une licence d&#x2019;activit&#xE9; apr&#xE8;s la r&#xE9;volutionau niveau local.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
